sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: fleet maintenance redesign 2026-11-03 (recipe.json read by Ansible, Tools phase last, recipe packages held). docs/reference/node-provisioning.md#converge-the-orbit-footprint.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: node:converge
  %% kind: node.converge
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Node 12<br/>reached over ssh
  participant H as VPN hub<br/>WireGuard peers
  CLI->>GW: node:converge 12
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:converge 12`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  Note over GW: Validate, lock Node + hub<br/>task #5180
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - Node 12 is an active, managed Linux Node
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - targets only: Node 12, its active roles, its Tools, its recorded network, and the hub
  %%> - no versions: the playbooks read them from the release's recipe.json
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-converge
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5180
  SW->>SW: Write the playbook input<br/>inventory · vars · known_hosts
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the intent is too large for one environment value, so it goes to a 0600 run file
  SW->>N: Install Orbit binaries<br/>ansible · tags binaries
  %%> Why first:
  %%> - later phases and Doctor rely on the agent's facts and the orbit-env group
  %%> - the CLI comes with it, so one converge brings a Node fully to the release
  SW->>N: Install role software<br/>ansible · tags software
  %%> Why:
  %%> - installs the recipe's common and role tools at their pins, then holds them
  %%> - the hold keeps Tools from moving tested software; Ubuntu `-security` updates still pass
  SW->>N: Configure the roles<br/>ansible · tags roles
  opt Node 12 has Tools
    SW->>N: Install Tools<br/>ansible · tags tools
    %%> Why last:
    %%> - a Tool that needs another version of a held package fails alone; role software stays as tested
    %%> On a Tool failure:
    %%> - the phase goes on with the other Tools and returns each Tool's result; the Gateway marks only that Tool failed
  end
  SW->>H: Apply the network<br/>ansible · network · Node + hub
  %%> Why one phase on both Nodes:
  %%> - the peer and the hub change together; Ansible runs them in parallel
  %%> - no drift writes no file and reloads nothing
  SW->>N: Check the Node<br/>ansible · tags check
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the one end check: role software, units, sites and a recent handshake
  alt check passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded
    Note over GW: Record converged state
    GW-->>CLI: Operation succeeded
  else a phase fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - nothing is rolled back; a rerun starts from the first phase and skips what matches
    Note over GW: Mark the task failed
    GW--xCLI: Operation failed
  end
